WEBVTT

00:00:00.281 --> 00:00:03.074
Last video ended here, with a cubic and

00:00:03.115 --> 00:00:04.461
its two derivative graphs.

00:00:05.428 --> 00:00:06.400
Now let's put them to work.

00:00:07.289 --> 00:00:09.963
This laptop shows a new video's total views,

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:10.787
day by day.

00:00:11.271 --> 00:00:14.186
They climb slowly at launch, then fast, then

00:00:14.468 --> 00:00:14.869
level off.

00:00:15.694 --> 00:00:18.001
From this graph alone, which day brought the

00:00:18.122 --> 00:00:19.325
most new views?

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.977
By the end, you'll read it straight off

00:00:21.998 --> 00:00:22.299
the shape.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.856
First, take a cubic you've met before,

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.949
y equals x cubed minus three x.

00:00:28.591 --> 00:00:30.552
It has a local maximum at minus one,

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:30.892
two,

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:33.393
a local minimum at one, minus two,

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:35.575
and an inflection at the origin.

00:00:36.262 --> 00:00:37.250
Are those points enough?

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.326
This wiggly curve goes through all three points.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.837
So does this one, made of straight lines.

00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:44.389
Both are wrong.

00:00:45.153 --> 00:00:46.856
What rules them out is what the derivatives

00:00:46.897 --> 00:00:48.018
say between the points:

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.161
constraints,

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.205
rules the curve has to obey.

00:00:51.768 --> 00:00:53.054
Start with f prime.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.871
f prime of x is three, times x

00:00:56.932 --> 00:00:59.180
minus one, times x plus one.

00:00:59.963 --> 00:01:02.226
It's positive when x is less than minus

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:02.467
one,

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.953
negative between minus one and one, and positive

00:01:05.995 --> 00:01:07.016
again after one.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:10.566
So the curve must rise, then fall, then

00:01:10.648 --> 00:01:10.927
rise.

00:01:11.872 --> 00:01:13.217
Now look at the wiggly curve.

00:01:13.941 --> 00:01:16.628
Near zero it climbs, where f prime says

00:01:16.669 --> 00:01:17.331
it must fall.

00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:18.647
So it's out.

00:01:19.475 --> 00:01:21.319
Each sign of f prime is a rule

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.465
for a whole interval, not just a point.

00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:26.336
f prime can't rule out the straight join.

00:01:27.082 --> 00:01:29.194
Now use f double prime, which is six

00:01:29.336 --> 00:01:29.396
x.

00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:32.350
For x less than zero it's negative, so

00:01:32.371 --> 00:01:34.559
the curve is concave down, bending like a

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:34.901
cap.

00:01:35.504 --> 00:01:38.338
For x greater than zero it's positive, concave

00:01:38.419 --> 00:01:39.223
up, like a cup.

00:01:39.987 --> 00:01:42.435
Straight lines don't bend, and they make sharp

00:01:42.496 --> 00:01:44.562
corners at minus one and one, where the

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:46.268
curve has to be smooth and flat.

00:01:47.213 --> 00:01:48.781
At the origin the bend changes,

00:01:49.305 --> 00:01:50.410
so that's the inflection.

00:01:50.993 --> 00:01:53.359
The gradient there is minus three, not zero,

00:01:53.721 --> 00:01:55.645
so it's a non-horizontal inflection.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:57.440
Now pin it down.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:58.696
Symmetry.

00:01:59.569 --> 00:02:02.180
f of minus x is minus f of

00:02:02.341 --> 00:02:03.787
x, so the function is odd.

00:02:04.471 --> 00:02:06.600
Give the right half a half turn about

00:02:06.621 --> 00:02:08.749
the origin, and it lands exactly on the

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.231
left half.

00:02:10.201 --> 00:02:10.666
Intercepts.

00:02:11.596 --> 00:02:14.580
x times x squared minus three is zero

00:02:14.761 --> 00:02:15.301
at zero,

00:02:15.803 --> 00:02:18.366
and at plus or minus root three, about

00:02:18.548 --> 00:02:19.428
one point seven three.

00:02:20.437 --> 00:02:21.063
And the ends.

00:02:21.731 --> 00:02:24.356
For large x, the x cubed term wins,

00:02:24.758 --> 00:02:26.440
so the curve heads up on the right,

00:02:26.762 --> 00:02:27.783
and down on the left.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:31.264
Label every feature, and only one shape fits.

00:02:31.927 --> 00:02:32.847
That's the whole checklist:

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:33.948
domain,

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:34.929
symmetry,

00:02:35.551 --> 00:02:37.332
intercepts, stationary points,

00:02:37.913 --> 00:02:39.274
concavity and inflections,

00:02:39.976 --> 00:02:42.417
asymptotes and other breaks, and what happens as

00:02:42.678 --> 00:02:43.779
x heads off to infinity.

00:02:44.642 --> 00:02:47.310
For a polynomial, the domain and asymptote checks

00:02:47.351 --> 00:02:47.972
take one line.

00:02:48.657 --> 00:02:49.964
The next curve needs all seven.

00:02:50.649 --> 00:02:53.424
Sketch y equals x plus one over x.

00:02:54.314 --> 00:02:54.923
Domain first.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.437
x can't be zero, so the graph has

00:02:57.478 --> 00:02:59.485
a gap there, and comes in two separate

00:02:59.506 --> 00:02:59.807
pieces.

00:03:00.671 --> 00:03:01.111
It's odd,

00:03:01.654 --> 00:03:04.241
since f of minus x is minus f

00:03:04.282 --> 00:03:04.562
of x.

00:03:05.486 --> 00:03:07.953
There are no intercepts, because x plus one

00:03:08.114 --> 00:03:10.682
over x equals zero would need x squared

00:03:10.803 --> 00:03:11.665
equals minus one.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.797
f prime of x is x squared minus

00:03:15.918 --> 00:03:17.181
one, over x squared,

00:03:17.804 --> 00:03:19.989
which is zero at one and minus one.

00:03:21.215 --> 00:03:23.808
f double prime is two over x cubed.

00:03:24.613 --> 00:03:27.301
At one it's positive, so one, two is

00:03:27.322 --> 00:03:27.903
a local minimum.

00:03:28.526 --> 00:03:31.035
At minus one it's negative, so minus one,

00:03:31.357 --> 00:03:33.163
minus two is a local maximum.

00:03:34.415 --> 00:03:36.858
Two over x cubed is negative on the

00:03:36.919 --> 00:03:39.423
left and positive on the right, so the

00:03:39.464 --> 00:03:41.887
concavity does change across zero.

00:03:42.429 --> 00:03:44.738
But zero isn't in the domain, so there's

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.109
no point there, and no inflection.

00:03:48.233 --> 00:03:50.437
As x gets close to zero from the

00:03:50.538 --> 00:03:53.763
right, one over x grows without limit, so

00:03:53.784 --> 00:03:54.565
f heads up.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.723
From the left, it heads down.

00:03:57.187 --> 00:04:00.176
So x equals zero is a vertical asymptote.

00:04:00.919 --> 00:04:03.343
And as x gets large, one over x

00:04:03.444 --> 00:04:06.129
shrinks towards zero, so the curve gets closer

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.972
to the line y equals x.

00:04:08.596 --> 00:04:10.386
Now go the other way, from a graph

00:04:10.408 --> 00:04:11.614
of f with no formula.

00:04:12.338 --> 00:04:13.903
f prime is the gradient of f.

00:04:14.749 --> 00:04:16.386
Line the graphs up, one under the other.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.662
Where f turns, the tangent is flat, so

00:04:19.783 --> 00:04:21.008
f prime is zero.

00:04:21.551 --> 00:04:22.473
Where f rises,

00:04:22.976 --> 00:04:24.461
f prime is above the axis.

00:04:25.005 --> 00:04:26.401
Where f falls, it's below.

00:04:27.026 --> 00:04:28.772
And f is falling most steeply at the

00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:30.981
origin, so that's the lowest point on f

00:04:31.283 --> 00:04:31.563
prime.

00:04:32.429 --> 00:04:33.059
Now do it again.

00:04:33.748 --> 00:04:35.374
f double prime is the gradient of f

00:04:35.736 --> 00:04:36.037
prime.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.303
f prime falls until x equals zero, then

00:04:39.364 --> 00:04:42.067
rises, so f double prime is negative, then

00:04:42.169 --> 00:04:45.072
positive, crossing zero right under the inflection.

00:04:45.656 --> 00:04:46.322
Back to the video.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:49.454
Daily views are the gradient of the total.

00:04:50.258 --> 00:04:52.443
At launch the total is nearly flat, so

00:04:52.544 --> 00:04:54.007
daily views start near zero.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.221
The total is steepest on day three, so

00:04:57.262 --> 00:04:59.070
that's the busiest day for new views.

00:04:59.975 --> 00:05:02.644
After that it still rises, but less steeply,

00:05:02.906 --> 00:05:05.033
so daily views fall away in a long

00:05:05.095 --> 00:05:05.355
tail.

00:05:06.119 --> 00:05:08.169
And day three is where the total switches

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.340
from concave up to concave down.

00:05:11.165 --> 00:05:12.931
The busiest day is the inflection.

00:05:13.737 --> 00:05:14.441
Here's a new graph.

00:05:15.106 --> 00:05:17.734
At x equals three it turns, so f

00:05:17.835 --> 00:05:20.243
prime crosses the axis there, from negative to

00:05:20.284 --> 00:05:20.644
positive.

00:05:21.368 --> 00:05:24.095
But at the origin, the curve flattens and

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:24.898
keeps falling.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.525
The tangent is flat, so f prime is

00:05:27.566 --> 00:05:29.811
zero, but its sign doesn't change.

00:05:30.415 --> 00:05:32.325
The graph of f prime touches the axis

00:05:32.547 --> 00:05:33.491
and goes back down.

00:05:33.995 --> 00:05:35.753
That's a horizontal point of inflection.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:38.607
The curve also changes its bend at x

00:05:38.648 --> 00:05:40.556
equals two, while it's still falling.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.119
There, f prime has a turning point.

00:05:43.644 --> 00:05:45.417
It also turns at zero, where it touches.

00:05:45.962 --> 00:05:48.330
So f double prime crosses zero at both

00:05:48.392 --> 00:05:48.652
points.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.024
Turns drop to zeros.

00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:54.491
Every turning point on one graph sits directly

00:05:54.572 --> 00:05:56.553
above a zero on the next graph down.

00:05:57.296 --> 00:05:59.545
A zero that crosses means a turn above

00:05:59.566 --> 00:05:59.625
it.

00:06:00.309 --> 00:06:02.751
A zero that only touches means a flat

00:06:02.812 --> 00:06:03.952
point that doesn't turn.

00:06:04.615 --> 00:06:06.704
This works on any smooth piece of curve.

00:06:09.339 --> 00:06:09.784
Your turn.

00:06:10.475 --> 00:06:12.835
For f of x equals x minus four

00:06:12.876 --> 00:06:13.356
over x,

00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:15.617
state the domain and the symmetry,

00:06:16.298 --> 00:06:18.058
show that there are no stationary points,

00:06:18.699 --> 00:06:20.499
and decide whether the curve has a point

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.220
of inflection.

00:06:21.884 --> 00:06:22.709
Pause here to answer.

00:06:33.615 --> 00:06:35.886
The domain is x not equal to zero,

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.333
and f is odd.

00:06:38.258 --> 00:06:40.659
f prime of x is one plus four

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:43.582
over x squared, which is always positive, so

00:06:43.623 --> 00:06:45.904
the curve rises on each piece and never

00:06:45.945 --> 00:06:46.264
turns.

00:06:47.109 --> 00:06:49.382
f double prime is minus eight over x

00:06:49.483 --> 00:06:49.885
cubed.

00:06:50.469 --> 00:06:52.857
It changes sign across zero, but zero isn't

00:06:52.938 --> 00:06:53.499
in the domain.

00:06:54.083 --> 00:06:55.732
No point, so no inflection.

00:06:57.389 --> 00:06:57.798
Last one.

00:06:58.586 --> 00:07:00.540
The graph of y equals f of x

00:07:00.761 --> 00:07:01.124
is shown.

00:07:02.286 --> 00:07:04.128
Where is f prime of x equal to

00:07:04.168 --> 00:07:04.508
zero,

00:07:05.309 --> 00:07:07.111
and does the graph of f prime cross

00:07:07.251 --> 00:07:08.873
or touch the axis at each one?

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:12.022
Then, where does the graph of f prime

00:07:12.102 --> 00:07:13.206
have its turning points?

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:14.978
Pause here to answer.

00:07:25.648 --> 00:07:28.133
f is flat at minus one and at

00:07:28.215 --> 00:07:30.660
two, so f prime is zero there.

00:07:31.463 --> 00:07:33.787
At minus one, f turns from falling to

00:07:33.869 --> 00:07:35.912
rising, so f prime crosses.

00:07:36.836 --> 00:07:39.983
At two, f flattens but keeps rising, so

00:07:40.124 --> 00:07:41.246
f prime only touches.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.575
f prime turns where f changes its bend,

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.320
at zero and at two.

00:07:47.124 --> 00:07:49.657
And f crossing the axis at zero doesn't

00:07:49.698 --> 00:07:51.044
make f prime zero there.

00:07:52.727 --> 00:07:54.869
So a sketch is a set of constraints,

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.112
and the derivatives supply most of them.

00:07:57.876 --> 00:07:59.867
Next, you build the function yourself, from a

00:07:59.929 --> 00:08:00.753
real situation.

00:08:01.578 --> 00:08:03.825
Forty metres of fencing make three sides of

00:08:03.866 --> 00:08:05.751
a sheep pen, against a stone wall.

00:08:06.294 --> 00:08:08.224
Which shape gives the largest area?

00:08:10.917 --> 00:08:11.785
Here are the key notes.

00:08:12.352 --> 00:08:13.785
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:14.290
to copy them.
